    writing-runbooks: add executable-checklist structure for runbook bodies
    
    On-call engineers couldn't execute runbooks mid-incident because diagnosis
    commentary was woven together with the commands to run. Add a recipe for
    the runbook body: a per-step contract (imperative action -> command ->
    expected result -> branch) and a Background block that holds the why/story
    so the steps stay scannable and executable under pressure.

